{
  "mn38:0.1": "Middle Discourses 38 ",
  "mn38:0.2": "The Longer Discourse on the Ending of Craving ",
  "mn38:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn38:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn38:2.1": "Now at that time a mendicant named Sāti, the fisherman’s son, had the following harmful misconception: ",
  "mn38:2.2": "“As I understand the Buddha’s teaching, it is this very same consciousness that roams and transmigrates, not another.” ",
  "mn38:3.1": "Several mendicants heard this rumour. ",
  "mn38:3.2": "",
  "mn38:3.3": "",
  "mn38:3.4": "They went up to Sāti and said to him, ",
  "mn38:3.5": "“Is it really true, Reverend Sāti, that you have such a harmful misconception: ",
  "mn38:3.6": "‘As I understand the Buddha’s teaching, it is this very same consciousness that roams and transmigrates, not another’?” ",
  "mn38:3.7": "“Indeed, reverends. As I understand the Buddha’s teaching, it is this very same consciousness that roams and transmigrates, not another.” ",
  "mn38:3.8": "Then, wishing to dissuade Sāti from his view, the mendicants pursued, pressed, and grilled him, ",
  "mn38:3.9": "“Don’t say that, Sāti! Don’t misrepresent the Buddha, for misrepresentation of the Buddha is not good. And the Buddha would not say that. ",
  "mn38:3.10": "In many ways the Buddha has said that consciousness is dependently originated, that without a cause, consciousness does not come to be.” ",
  "mn38:3.11":